A||||5||DR650SE||Fuel pump wiring problem, Please help||||8||
Z||000000||DR650SE||10-25-2001||03:05 PM||||Today I spent quite a while trying to get my fuel pump working which I have mailed the list about.  I tried the relay and everything but I think the problem lies in the orange/black wire.  The wireing diagram says that it should be hot at all times but it has no power at terminal D on the fuel pump relay.  I think it gets power from the orange wire thats a fusible link that is hot at all times.  PLease help.  Thanks<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||8
Z||000001||Gary W||10-25-2001||09:11 PM||||**Disclaimer** I am not a mechanic, but I play one in my garage. Anything you blow up is your problem.<P>The hot wire to the fuel pump relay is orange and black - pin "D" on the pump relay. Should read 12V to ground with ignition on. To check if your pump operates, do the following: Access the ALCL connector near the cigarette lighter. Apply 12V DC to test pin "G". On my '86, this is the pin closest to the driver on the top row. You can get 12V from the center (orange) wire of the cigarette lighter. You will hear the pump run, and if you can now start the engine, the pump is not your problem. My car had both a bad oil pressure switch and ECM, so the pump wouldn't run at all when cranking.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DR650SE||10-26-2001||01:04 AM||||I tried all that stuff but it tiurned out to be the relay and the fuse.  Im such and idiot.  Thanks for the help though||||reg||9
